Alembic migrations for Driftwatch.

The application runs `alembic upgrade head` on startup (see
`driftwatch.db.Database.upgrade`), so a fresh database is built and an existing
one is migrated forward automatically. A database that has tables but no Alembic
version is refused rather than stamped, because its schema cannot be verified.

The chain starts from a single 1.0 baseline. Databases created by development
builds before that baseline are not upgraded and must be created again.

To add a migration after changing the models:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
    # review the generated file in versions/, then
    alembic upgrade head

`env.py` reads the database URL from the application's settings and maps the
async driver to its synchronous peer (`psycopg` for PostgreSQL, installed from
the lock files), so no URL needs to be set in alembic.ini.
